<title>USA: Freeport-McMoRan Resource cuts payout.</title>
<headline>Freeport-McMoRan Resource cuts payout.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freeport-McMoRan Resource Partners LP said it declared a cash distribution for the quarter ended March 31, 1997 of $0.31 per unit, down from the previous quarterly payout of $0.60 per unit.</p>
<p>The distribution is payable May 15, 1997 to unitholders of record at the close of business on April 30, 1997.</p>
<p>Freeport said the cash distribution was determined by available distributable cash resulting from operations of the partnership and the terms of the partnership agreement.</p>
<p>It said that in the future, cash distributions will also be determined on this basis.  It had paid $0.60 per share on a regular quarterly basis.</p>
</text>
